background:
Tighten requirements to ensure only those actively seeking work or facing genuine barriers can access benefits;
Limit the duration of benefits for individuals capable of working;
Strengthen systems to detect and prevent fraud or misuse;

additional_details:
We urge the UK Government to reform the CMS by:

Introducing a minimum child maintenance payment for all, regardless of employment;

Tying support to cost of living and regional baselines, not just declared income;

Auditing lifestyle and assets, not only pay slips;

Stopping temporary overnight care claims as a loophole;

Enforcing stricter verification and consequences for manipulation.

We want this law to:
- Establish statutory protections and rights to secure payment and enable action in defence of life;
- Investigate possibly coercive practices within the private security industry;
- Create a public registry or ombudsman to oversee complaints and uphold professional standards in the sector.

When cabinet members are fiddling with their phones and giggling and mocking other members, it is totally disrespectful.
"To the end that all the Debates in this House should be grave and orderly, as becomes so great an Assembly; and that all Interruptions should be prevented;
Be it Ordered and Declared, That no Member of this House do presume to make any Noise or Disturbance, whilst any Member shall be orderly debating, or whilst any Bill, Order or other Matter, shall be in reading or opening."

Research by TSSA union found a prevalence of workplace violence experienced by transport workers:

- Over half of respondents reported experiencing physical or verbal violence in the past year;
- 95% of respondents reported receiving verbal threats or abuse;
- 40% of respondents reported incidents involving weapons.

The RSSB Health & Safety Report 2023/24 found that assaults on train staff have increased, despite passenger journeys not returning to pre-pandemic levels.

The English are the historic and ancestral population of England, with continuous cultural, linguistic, legal, and territorial presence dating back over a millennium. Like all indigenous peoples they have the right to:

-Maintain their distinct identity, cultural traditions, and institutions;

-Be protected from policies or demographic changes that threaten their survival as a distinct people.

An urgent inquiry is needed to assess the impact of high interest rates on productivity, consumer demand, housing, and public debt.
We are calling for:
	•	A 1% reduction in the Bank of England base rate to stimulate growth;
	•	Parliamentary oversight to ensure monetary policy reflects the UK’s real economic challenges;
	•	Government support in shaping a coordinated response to avoid a deeper downturn.

The UK cannot afford to wait. Please read, share, and—if you agree—sign.

background:
Conduct a full review of benefits, housing, and support currently accessible to illegal migrants;

Immediately suspend access to benefits and housing support for individuals with no legal right to remain in the UK;

Strengthen enforcement to ensure taxpayer money is not misallocated.

additional_details:
Increase the minimum wage specifically for domiciliary and community care workers;
Recognise care work as a professional, skilled role;
Set a national standard for care worker pay that reflects the value and responsibility of the job.
It’s time to value care—and the people who provide it Care work is not low-skilled—it requires training, compassion, patience, and resilience. We play a vital role in keeping people safe, well, and independent at home. This should be recognised with fair pay.

